{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the name of the slain woman, etc.</b> To inform you of the hatred of the Midianites — that they gave over a king's daughter to whoredom in order to make Israel sin." "<b>Head of the tribes.</b> One of the five kings of Midian — ״אֶת אֱוִי וְאֶת רֶקֶם וְאֶת צוּר״ etc. (Numbers 31:8) — and he was the most distinguished of them all, as it says ״רֹאשׁ אֻמּוֹת״; and because he conducted himself with degradation, giving over his own daughter, he is counted third." "<b>A father's house.</b> Midian had five father's houses: ״עֵיפָה וָעֵפֶר וַחֲנֹךְ וַאֲבִידָע וְאֶלְדָּעָה״ (Genesis 25) — and this one was king over one of them."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:48.322725832Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}